# Whale Girl — Low-Memory Discipline

- Budgets (tech-stack.md): server ≤ 60 MB RSS, Python driver ≤ 30 MB RSS at 30 FPS.
  Re-measure with
  ps -axo pid,rss,command | grep -E 'node server.js|control_whale.py' at every
  feature close.
- Hot paths must not allocate per frame: the driver's frame dict is pre-allocated and
  mutated in place; the frontend message handler avoids closures/spreads; the server
  never JSON.parses frames (raw-text passthrough).
- No per-frame logging; aggregate logs only (server every 5 s, driver every 1 s).
- No Electron, no heavy UI libraries, no heavy Python deps (no numpy/scipy/GUI).
- CDN dependencies stay pinned to the exact verified versions in tech-stack.md
  (PixiJS 7.4.3, pixi-live2d-display 0.4.0, Cubism Core official URL).
- New Python dependencies must declare their Python-version ceiling (the Mac runs
  3.9.10; websockets is capped at <16 for that reason).
